RESULT
========================================================================
PASS: tr(rho(a)) for M_CKM=m006(-5,2), computed via a CERTIFIED
(interval-arithmetic, not algdep) holonomy representation, is proven
via interval-Newton contraction to lie in a box containing EXACTLY
ONE root of qa(x)=p(-x), well-separated (distance > 1e-3, vs. box
radius ~2^-280) from all 9 other roots.

This is a substantial rigor upgrade over algdep-based recognition:
an explicit, arbitrarily-improvable numerical certificate with a
provable error bound, via interval Newton -- NOT yet a symbolic/exact
algebraic proof that tr(rho(a)) is EXACTLY a root of qa (that would
require an exact identity on the character variety, as in Q-001).

